/* A char literal is one UTF-16 code unit, and `'😀'` is two.

   javac 21 accepts it anyway and takes the pair's first code unit (the program
   below compiles there and prints 55357); Teyru rejects it, which is what the
   .code file beside this one pins. Whether the two should agree is a decision
   for the owner: the plan's W7 item 6 assumed javac reports an error here, and
   on JDK 21 it does not. */
class EmojiCharLiteral {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    char c = '😀'
    System.out.println((int) c)
  }
}
